  "summary": "Pflugerville voters approved most of 14 proposed city charter amendments in Nov. 3 unofficial results, rejecting Props A, C, H and L. Among the approved measures was Proposition B, which requires the City Council to adopt rules protecting resident privacy when the city uses data collection, facial recognition, surveillance tools and AI, and mandates a public approval process before such technologies are deployed.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Proposition B: Requires the City Council to adopt rules that protect residents' privacy when the city collects and uses data, facial recognition, surveillance tools and artificial intelligence. It also requires a public approval process before these technologies are used and establishes standards for their responsible use. For: 76.6% Against: 23.1%",
      "paragraph_idx": 9
    }
  ],
